# Refactoring

Use this when replacing a tangled implementation or moving code between directories.

## Do

- Split along responsibilities (I/O, policy, state, UI). Prefer composition over a new god-object.
- After moves, code should still look like siblings (`tree-style.mdc`). Headers stay next to `.cc` (`colocated-sources.mdc`).
- Update **`BUILD.gn` sources**, includes, and any path-scoped rules in the **same change**.

## Don’t

- Don’t chunk a file only by line count.
- Don’t introduce Qt, WinUI, WebView2, or CEF while reshaping (`no-qt.mdc`).
- Don’t rewrite `skia/` or `third_party/` as part of a product refactor.
